ralph/progress.txt:27388:  - The SECURITY.md substring matcher set MUST include `FOR UPDATE` (the lock the hard-limit invariant rests on) and `organization_id` (the predicate the cross-tenant invariant rests on) — these are the two load-bearing engine details an auditor must see to verify the invariant from the documented contract alone, without opening the test file. The 13-substring set is the minimum that pins every BE-0384 AC.
ralph/progress.txt:36613:- What was implemented: Added the versioned pricing plan catalog schema and repository. Migration `0049_pricing_plan_catalog` creates `plans`, `plan_entitlements`, `pricing_plan_status`, and `pricing_billing_period`; seeds Starter, Pro, Business, and Enterprise monthly v1 packages; and seeds entitlements covering hard, soft, metered, and disabled enforcement modes. `PricingPlanRepository` now supports create, exact-version reads, active listing, update-by-archive-and-new-version, archive, entitlement upsert, and entitlement listing.
ralph/progress.txt:36620:  - `PricingPlanRepository.Update` must close the entitlement read cursor before writing cloned entitlements in the same transaction; pgx transactions cannot run another statement while rows from the previous query are still open.
ralph/progress.txt:36621:  - `plan_entitlements` intentionally uses free-form `entitlement_key` with `quota_enforcement_mode` because pricing/metering dimensions extend beyond the existing `quota_resource` domain.
ralph/progress.txt:36624:- What was implemented: Added subscription and entitlement override persistence plus the deterministic runtime resolver. Migration `0050_subscriptions_entitlement_overrides` creates `subscriptions`, `subscription_entitlements`, `subscription_status`, and `subscription_entitlement_source`; `SubscriptionRepository` now creates accepted-plan rows, upserts effective-windowed overrides, resolves entitlements by precedence, and exposes a `PlanLookup` for current subscriptions.
ralph/progress.txt:36625:- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0050_subscriptions_entitlement_overrides.up.sql`, `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0050_subscriptions_entitlement_overrides.down.sql`, `internal/controlplane/store/subscription.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/subscription_repository_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/subscription_schema_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/AGENTS.md`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
ralph/progress.txt:36630:  - Current subscription entitlement reads should ignore `canceled` and out-of-period rows; those rows are historical/audit anchors, not runtime access grants.
ralph/progress.txt:36631:  - `subscription_entitlements.source` enforces shape: `subscription_override` rows must carry a tenant-scoped subscription id, while `emergency_admin` rows are organization-level and must leave `subscription_id` null.
ralph/progress.txt:36645:- What was implemented: Added the production entitlement resolver service in `internal/controlplane/entitlements`. The resolver wraps `store.SubscriptionRepository`, returns deterministic keyed snapshots with source/value/enforcement/explanation fields, validates cache entries with `EntitlementRevision`, and exposes `ResolveWithQuerier` for in-transaction quota/worker/billing use. `quota.Checker` now accepts `quota.WithEntitlementResolver` and prefers entitlement keys matching quota resources before falling back to legacy `quota_policies`. `cmd/yalla-api` wires `SubscriptionRepository.PlanLookup` into limits/usage readers and the entitlement resolver into the shared quota checker used by mutating unit-of-work services.
ralph/progress.txt:36646:- Files changed: `cmd/yalla-api/main.go`, `internal/controlplane/entitlements/resolver.go`, `internal/controlplane/entitlements/resolver_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/quota/quota.go`, `internal/controlplane/quota/quota_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/subscription.go`, `internal/controlplane/AGENTS.md`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
ralph/progress.txt:36657:  - Extended `GET /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits` to return customer-visible entitlement-backed limits with current usage, billing-period reset windows, source labels, and warning thresholds while preserving legacy quota-policy fallback.
ralph/progress.txt:36659:  - Added store read composition that prefers current accepted subscription entitlements, joins `quota_usage`, filters to known quota resources, sorts deterministically, and avoids exposing provider ids, plan ids, subscription ids, override ids, or override reasons.
ralph/progress.txt:36701:  - Keep the limits/usage reader fallback path: current subscriptions use `subscriptions` + `plan_entitlements` + `subscription_entitlements`; organizations without a current subscription still use legacy `quota_policies`.
ralph/progress.txt:36968:  - Retry build time should sum immutable `job_attempts`; cancelled attempts still contribute elapsed worker time, but cancelled deployments should not consume the successful/failed deployment-count entitlement key.
